  message: "Materialized from dogfood tranche 05 (F81.A1 / anon-card-014). Mechanism: calls-edge src endpoint resolves to wrong same-base-name sibling. Evidence: frozen substrate.json — 506/110510 calls edges out-of-span; concrete probe at io_boundary.py:939-954 (BoundaryMap.to_dict) vs true owner IoChain.to_dict at 855-870, call line 863. Magnitude: 506 edges, 201 src methods, 68 files; 504/506 (99.6%) attributed to same-base-name peer; 100% of src base names have multiplicity >1. Blind severity 5/5, reproduced on frozen substrate (read-only join, no injection). RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT from INV-majal (Go local-var-as-method-reference, holding), INV-mofav (Python nested-fn/bare-name-call drops, satisfied), and the various analyzer single-value-dict same-name resolution items (Go/Rust/verilog, done) — those are node-level/analyzer resolution defects; this is an edge-attribution defect where the calls EDGE src endpoint resolves to the wrong same-named peer in the same file."  # 2875
